Description: Fits area-level geoadditive small area estimation (SAE)
    models, extending the Fay-Herriot (FH) model to allow linear,
    nonlinear, and spatial effects. Nonlinear covariate effects are
    represented using penalized splines, while spatial effects are
    represented using a smooth function of geographic coordinates.
    Models are estimated using restricted maximum likelihood (REML),
    and mean squared error (MSE) is estimated using a parametric
    bootstrap. The package also provides comparisons with the
    Fay-Herriot and spatial Fay-Herriot (SFH) models.
References: Fay and Herriot (1979) <doi:10.1080/01621459.1979.10482505>;
    Ruppert (2002) <doi:10.1198/016214502188618529>;
    Pusponegoro et al. (2019) <doi:10.21108/JDSA.2019.2.15>;
    Wood (2025) <doi:10.1146/annurev-statistics-112723-034249>
